alt-syscall: allow rseq, clone3, faccessat2, close_range and pidfd_open in "complete"

A current glibc and dbus call all five on every process start or on common
paths (rseq registration at startup, clone3 for posix_spawn/pthread_create,
faccessat2 for access()/test -x, close_range in exec helpers, pidfd_open in
dbus-daemon and at-spi-bus-launcher to watch their children). Under the
enforcing "complete" table each one hit block_syscall(), which returns
-ENOSYS; userspace falls back, so nothing broke, but every process start
logged "blocked syscall 334/434/435/436/439" and flooded dmesg.

The entries go in the section shared by all architectures: the table is
keyed on __NR_<name>, and all five exist on both x86_64 (334, 434, 435,
436, 439) and arm64 (asm-generic: 293, 434, 435, 436, 439), so this
covers both. The compat (32-bit) whitelist is unchanged.
